2. CSS units — sizing everything

Unit	        Meaning	                                                                Best use
px	            CSS pixels	                                                            Borders, small precise dimensions
%	            Relative to a containing dimension, depending on property	            Flexible widths
em	            Relative to the element's font size(or inherited font size for some properties)	Component-relative sizing
rem	            Relative to the root font size	                                        Consistent spacing and typography
vw	            1% of viewport width	                                                Viewport-based sizing
vh	            1% of viewport height	                                                Viewport-height layouts
dvh	            1% of dynamic viewport height	                                        Mobile full-height sections
vmin / vmax	    1% of smaller / larger viewport dimension	                            Responsive scaling
ch	            Width of the 0 glyph in the relevant font	                            Text line width
fr	            Fraction of available grid space	                                    CSS Grid columns
auto	        Browser calculates the value according to the property	                Automatic sizing or margins




3. The CSS box model
Every HTML element is treated as a box. Understanding this is essential because nearly every UI layout uses it.
Margin — outside space
Border
Padding — inside space
Content

Conceptual illustration of the CSS box model.
Property	Purpose	                            Example
width	    Content width by default	        width: 300px;
height	    Content height by default	        height: 200px;
min-width	Minimum width	                    min-width: 200px;
max-width	Maximum width	                    max-width: 1200px;
min-height	Minimum height	                    min-height: 100vh;
max-height	Maximum height	                    max-height: 500px;
margin	    Outside spacing	                    margin: 20px;
padding	    Inside spacing	                    padding: 16px;
border	    Border around the element	        border: 1px solid #ddd;
box-sizing	How width and height are calculated	border-box



Modern logical alternatives are useful for different writing directions:
.card {
  margin-block: 20px;       /* start and end vertically */
  padding-inline: 16px;     /* left/right in typical English */
  margin-inline: auto;      /* commonly centers a fixed-width block */
}


Why box-sizing matters
*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}


With border-box, declared width includes content, padding and border.
This makes sizing easier to predict and is a common global default.